    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24328" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δηλ-ήμων</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, gen.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ονος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>baneful, noxious,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βροτῶν δηλήμονα πάντων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					18.85
				</span></i>
			, al.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄφιες ἀνθρώπων οὐδαμῶς
				δηλήμονες</span>
			<i>doing</i> men no <i>hurt,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.74
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				3.109
			</span></i>: abs., of the gods, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σχέτλιοί ἐστε, θεοί, δηλήμονες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					24.33
				</span></i>
			 (in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				5.118
			</span></i> nearly all codd. give <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζηλήμονες</span>): in late Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Or.</u>
				2.87a
			</span></i>.</div>
